    <briefdescription>
<para>An implementation of <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_binary_stream" kindref="compound">BinaryStream</ref> whose data is backed by an llvm <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_memory_buffer" kindref="compound">MemoryBuffer</ref> object. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_memory_buffer_byte_stream" kindref="compound">MemoryBufferByteStream</ref> owns the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_memory_buffer" kindref="compound">MemoryBuffer</ref> in question. As with <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_binary_byte_stream" kindref="compound">BinaryByteStream</ref>, reading from a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_memory_buffer_byte_stream" kindref="compound">MemoryBufferByteStream</ref> will never cause a copy. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
